# Storylines (AutonomousBotStorylines, 2026-10-26, the owner's idea). Multi-day dramas between two bots, played in
# /faction as episodes a few days apart. The same two bots play roles A and B in every episode of an arc; roles C-H are
# other bots of the realm each time (bystanders, gossips, peacemakers, instigators). {name_a} and {name_b} are the two
# protagonists' names, so everyone names them. A real player may take a side in faction: the last episode then plays as
# _4a (the player sided with A) or _4b (with B), and {player} is that player. Plain _4 is the ending nobody chose. Each
# arc starts fun and turns spicy fast, with callbacks to the earlier episodes. Afterwards the protagonist the player
# backed sends a "side_thanks" tell, the one they went against a "side_scorn" tell ({target} is the rival's name).
# Real swear words are not in the corpus: they swear the way 2003 chat did, wtf, stfu, gtfo, omfg, $#@!. New writing.

@kind debate
@realm *

# ==== killsteal: B took a named kill A had camped for an hour ======================================

@topic story_killsteal
@levels 10-50
@scene story_killsteal_1
@role A type=Leveler levels=10-50
@role B type=Daredevil levels=10-50
@role C type=*
@role D type=*
@role E type=Socialite
@role F type=*
@role G type=*
@role H type=NoLifer
A: omg. i camped that named for a FULL HOUR and {name_b} just ran in and took it | an hour. sixty minutes. the named pops and {name_b} tags it out of nowhere
C: lol rip | oof
D: classic | welcome to camp life
B: lol what? it was up, i hit it. thats how named mobs work {name_a} | {name_a} it was just standing there. first hit wins. thats the rule
A: i was sitting RIGHT THERE {name_b}. you ran past me. you SAW me | {name_b} you literally ran past my campfire to get to it
B: i saw someone sitting. i figured you were afk | you were sitting down. i thought you fell asleep
A: i was MEDDING. for the PULL. that i was going to MAKE | i was resting up for the pull i had waited an hour to make
E: {name_b} did you at least say sorry | did {name_b} even type a sorry
B: sorry the named liked me better | sorry {name_a}. sorry you're slow
F: ohhh | OHHHH
G: {name_b} just went for it | {name_b} woke up and chose chaos
A: what did it even drop. tell me it dropped junk | please tell me it dropped nothing at least
B: oh it dropped the good one. looks great on me | the rare. first kill. feels amazing actually
A: you are kidding me | are you serious right now
H: an hour is an hour, {name_b}. thats {name_a}'s camp | sorry {name_b}, camp rules say {name_a} had it
B: camp rules are made up by people who are slow on the draw | theres no camp rules. theres fast and theres slow
A: ok. ok {name_b}. i'll remember this | noted {name_b}. noted. i have a long memory
B: remember it while i wear the loot lol | remember what? the loot? its on my back now
D: this is going to be a thing isnt it | i smell a feud
E: {name_a} vs {name_b}, round one | someone start a log, this one is going places
A: next time it pops, you better be nowhere near it {name_b} | if i see you near my camp again {name_b}, we have a problem
B: or what {name_a}? you'll med at me? | ooh scary. what are you going to do, sit at me harder?
F: rofl sit at me harder | lol "med at me"
~ 6
H: note to self: never sit down near {name_b} | everyone guard your camps, {name_b} is loose

