# ==== guildsplit: A leads a guild, B is an officer; loot rules split it ===========================

@topic story_guildsplit
@levels 10-50
@scene story_guildsplit_1
@role A type=Socialite levels=10-50
@role B type=NoLifer levels=10-50
@role C type=*
@role D type=Crafter
@role E type=*
@role F type=*
@role G type=*
@role H type=*
B: ok since {name_a} wont listen in guild chat: we need loot rules. real ones | posting this in faction so the whole realm sees: {name_a}, our guild needs a loot system
A: lol {name_b} why is this in faction. we have guild chat for this | {name_b}... we have a guild channel. you know that right
B: because in guild chat you just type "lol" and go afk | you ignore me in guild chat. here you cant
C: oh no, guild drama in faction. my favorite | grabbing a snack, guild fight in faction
A: our loot system is fine. everyone rolls. its fun | free rolls for everyone. its worked for months
B: its not fine. last raid someone who showed up for five minutes won the best drop | your "fun" gave the best drop to someone who logged in for the last pull
A: thats what rolls are, {name_b}. luck | thats luck {name_b}. sometimes the dice like people
B: i've been at every raid for months. the dice hate me | i've been to every single raid. my rolls are cursed
D: just use points. points for showing up, spend them on loot | points system. show up, earn points, spend them. easy
A: points are for boring guilds. we're a FUN guild | ugh, points. spreadsheets. we play to have fun, not to do math
B: fun for who? the one who showed up for five minutes? | fun for the people who roll in at the last pull, sure
E: {name_b} has a point honestly | i'm with {name_b}, showing up should count for something
F: nah {name_a} is right, points guilds are miserable | points guilds argue about points all day. {name_a} is right
A: ty. see {name_b}, the realm agrees with me | see, half the realm agrees with me {name_b}
B: half the realm isnt in our guild {name_a}. and they dont get robbed every raid | half the realm doesnt do our raids, {name_a}
G: wait is {name_b} an officer? arguing with their own leader in public lol | is {name_b} an officer? this is a mutiny
A: yes, and a good one usually. until today | {name_b} is my best officer. usually. not today
B: then listen to your best officer. points or i walk | then listen to me for once {name_a}. a real system, or else
A: or else what lol | ooh, or else. ok {name_b}
B: you'll see | try me
H: i give this guild two weeks | this guild has a countdown on it now
C: guild drama, season one. tune in next time | {name_a} vs {name_b}. part one of many, i bet

